  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Housing and Popular Organisation - S&#xE3;o Paulo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Urban Community Development programme aims to improve the quality of housing and basic services for low-income families living in the shanty towns and tenement blocks of Sao Paulo, Brazil&#x2019;s largest city.   To do this, it will use three strategies: advocacy, campaigning and capacity building at the grassroots.  The programme will be implemented by organisations with long years of experience who have already achieved important gains in improving the government&#x2019;s housing policies.   All organizations have close links with the Church or are part of the Church&#x2019;s structures,
The three programmatic lines of the programme are as follows:
a)	The guarantee of urban public policy for housing that will benefit low income families.
b)	Strong participation of women and young people who live in the Favelas and poor areas of the city in consultation and decision making forums for the city.
c)	strong capacity and increased impact of local organisations in the defence of the right to housing and more inclusive and less violent city.</narrative>
  </description>
